<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretariat November grain shipment figures (tonnes), followed by January-November totals (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Wheat	383,763   (47,309)     3,969,760  (6,141,908)</p>
<p> Maize	252,524  (146,516)     6,760,518  (5,916,260)</p>
<p> Sorghum	5,250	(nil)	 665,804    (183,405)</p>
<p> Barley	   nil	(nil)	   6,888     (21,400)</p>
<p> Soybeans    43,000   (21,153)     2,114,283  (2,607,999)</p>
<p> Sunseed    131,000	(nil)	 537,374    (824,389)</p>
<p> Others	23,363    (9,898)	 261,644    (231,843)</p>
<p>Principal destinations in November were as follows (tonnes):  </p>
<p>WHEAT: Brazil 205,738; Turkey 51,900; Tunisia 41,750; Morocco 25,675; Kenya 22,550</p>
<p>MAIZE: Brazil 63,809; Britain 42,271; Iran 33,000; Cuba 28,830; Peru 26,375; Spain 22,000.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
